** Given, \(\ y = Ae^{3x} + Be^{5x}\)

On differentiating both sides w.r.t. \(x\), we get \(\frac{dy}{dx} = 3Ae^{3x} + 5Be^{5x}\)

\(\begin{matrix}
 & \  \Rightarrow \ y_{1} = 3Ae^{3x} + 5Be^{5x}\begin{bmatrix}
\ldots(ii) \\
\left\lbrack \because\frac{dy}{dx} = y_{1} \right\rbrack
\end{bmatrix} \\
 & \  \Rightarrow \ y_{2} = 9Ae^{3x} + 25Be^{5x}\ \ldots(iii)
\end{matrix}\)

Eliminating \(A\) and \(B\) in Eqs. (i), (ii) and (iii), we get

\(\begin{matrix}
\left| \begin{matrix}
e^{3x} & e^{5x} & - y \\
3e^{3x} & 5e^{5x} & - y_{1} \\
9e^{3x} & 25e^{5x} & - y^{2}
\end{matrix} \right| = 0 \\
 \Rightarrow ( - 1)e^{3x} \cdot e^{5x}\left| \begin{matrix}
1 & 1 & y \\
3 & 5 & y_{1} \\
9 & 25 & y_{2}
\end{matrix} \right| = 0
\end{matrix}\)

\(\begin{matrix}
 & \  \Rightarrow \ \left| \begin{matrix}
1 & 1 & y \\
3 & 5 & y_{1} \\
9 & 25 & y_{2}
\end{matrix} \right| = 0 \\
 & \  \Rightarrow 1\left( 2y_{2} - 16y_{1} \right) + y(48 - 18) = 0 \\
